# Persistence & Integration Rules

## Postgres via Prisma (system of record)

- Use Prisma schema for Postgres.
- Migrations must be generated (do not rely on "push" only).
- All primary keys UUID.
- Normalize transactional tables to 3NF where applicable.

## Redis (cache / locks / rate limits only)

- Redis must NOT be used as system of record.
- Allowed use: rate limiting, locks, cache.

## Kafka (primary event bus)

- Produce events using a dedicated adapter in infrastructure.
- Use a consistent event envelope (per docs/architecture/event-catalog.md).
- Consumers must be idempotent (at-least-once delivery).

## Outbox Pattern Preference

- Prefer implementing outbox table + background publisher.
- If omitted in the first iteration:
  - Document the trade-off in docs and service README.
